      <div class="wb-logo">World Bank Group</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Metrics Banner -->
  <div class="metrics-banner">
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number accent">6 Decades</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Strongest post-recession recovery in six decades</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number">1.2 Billion</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Youth entering working age in the next decade</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number teal">1.5 Billion</div>
      <div class="metric-label">People targeted for quality, affordable health services by 2030</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number teal">300 Million</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Electricity access target — Sub-Saharan Africa (Mission 300)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number">300 Million</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Farmers to move up the agricultural value chain (AgriConnect)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number">80 Million</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Women & women-led businesses to gain access to capital</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-number teal">1 Billion+</div>
      <div class="metric-label">People gaining improved water security (400M WBG commitment)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Content -->
  <div class="content-area" style="top: 372px; gap: 28px;">
    <!-- Section 1: Recovery -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-icon blue">📈</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>A Historic Recovery — But Uneven</h2>
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p>The global economy has demonstrated notable resilience in the face of heightened trade tensions and policy uncertainty. Last year's faster-than-expected growth capped a recovery from the 2020 recession that is <strong>unmatched in six decades</strong>. However, this headline resilience masks a widening gap: vulnerable emerging market and developing economies (EMDEs) continue to lag significantly behind advanced economies. Global growth is projected to edge downward this year, driven by firms scaling back inventory accumulation and the intensifying effects of tariffs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <hr class="section-divider">

    <!-- Section 2: Risks — STRONG VISUAL WEIGHT -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-icon rose">⚠️</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Risks to the Outlook</h2>
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;">Growth could falter further if trade tensions escalate or financial market sentiment deteriorates sharply. The following risks demand urgent policy attention:</p>
        <div class="risk-cards">
          <div class="risk-card">
            <h4>🔴 Trade Tensions & Tariffs</h4>
            <p>Escalation of tariffs and retaliatory measures could disrupt global supply chains and dampen investment across advanced and developing economies alike.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card amber-border">
            <h4>🟡 Financial Volatility</h4>
            <p>A sharp deterioration in market sentiment could tighten financing conditions, especially for EMDEs dependent on external capital flows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card" style="background:#f0f9ff; border-left-color:#0050a0;">
            <h4>🔵 Inventory Correction</h4>
            <p>Firms that front-loaded purchases are now drawing down stocks, reducing near-term demand and slowing industrial production.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card" style="background:#f0fdfa; border-left-color:#0096a0;">
            <h4>🟢 Climate Shocks</h4>
            <p>Extreme weather events continue to threaten agricultural output and critical infrastructure in the most vulnerable regions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <hr class="section-divider">

    <!-- Section 3: Policy Actions -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-icon amber">🏛️</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Policy Actions for Sustained Growth</h2>
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p>Global and domestic action is essential to sustain the recovery and foster inclusive job creation.</p>
        <div class="policy-grid">
          <div class="policy-item">
            <h4>Trade</h4>
            <p>Improve multilateral trade environment; diversify trade partners and products</p>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item">
            <h4>Finance</h4>
            <p>Ease external financing constraints for EMDEs; strengthen policy frameworks</p>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item">
            <h4>Climate</h4>
            <p>Scale up climate risk mitigation; invest in resilient infrastructure</p>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item">
            <h4>Investment</h4>
            <p>Catalyze private capital flows; remove structural bottlenecks to business entry</p>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item">
            <h4>Jobs</h4>
            <p>Support cross-border labor mobility; enhance skills and labor market flexibility</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <hr class="section-divider">

    <!-- Section 4: 2030 Strategic Priorities -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-icon teal">🎯</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>World Bank 2030 Strategic Priorities</h2>
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p>With <strong>1.2 billion young people</strong> reaching working age in the next decade, job creation is central to the World Bank Group's mission. The Bank has set ambitious targets across five flagship initiatives:</p>
        <div class="targets-grid">
          <div class="target-card">
            <div class="target-num">1.5B</div>
            <div class="target-label">Quality, affordable health services</div>
          </div>
          <div class="target-card">
            <div class="target-num teal">300M</div>
            <div class="target-label">Sub-Saharan Africa electricity access</div>
          </div>
          <div class="target-card">
            <div class="target-num">300M</div>
            <div class="target-label">Farmers moving up the agricultural value chain</div>
          </div>
          <div class="target-card">
            <div class="target-num teal">80M</div>
            <div class="target-label">Women & women-led businesses — capital access</div>
          </div>
          <div class="target-card">
            <div class="target-num">1B+</div>
            <div class="target-label">People with improved water security</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <hr class="section-divider">

    <!-- Section 5: Research Themes -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-icon navy">📚</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2>Key Research Themes in Recent Issues</h2>
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p>The Global Economic Prospects report series provides rigorous analysis on recurring challenges, underpinning the Bank's policy recommendations.</p>
        <div class="research-list">
          <span class="research-tag">Fiscal Policy & Fiscal Rules</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Trade Costs & Global Value Chains</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Commodity Price Cycles</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Financial Spillovers</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Pandemic Economics & Inequality</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Small States — Fiscal Challenges</span>
          <span class="research-tag">Debt Buildup Dynamics</span>
          <span class="research-tag">U.S. Interest Rate Impacts</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <div class="poster-footer">
    <span>Source: World Bank Group — Global Economic Prospects Report Series &nbsp;|&nbsp; Data as of 2025 &nbsp;|&nbsp; worldbank.org/gep</span>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
// Export button for PNG/SVG conversion
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
  const btn = document.createElement('button');
  btn.textContent = 'Export PNG';
  btn.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;top:10px;right:10px;z-index:9999;padding:10px 20px;background:#0050a0;color:#fff;border:none;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;';
  btn.onclick = function() {
    // Use canvas-based approach for PNG export
    const poster = document.getElementById('poster');
    const svgData = '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="' + poster.offsetWidth + '" height="' + poster.offsetHeight + '">' +
      '<foreignObject width="100%" height="100%">' +
      '<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">' + poster.outerHTML + '</div>' +
      '</foreignObject></svg>';
    const blob = new Blob([svgData], {type: 'image/svg+xml'});
    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    const img = new Image();
    img.onload = function() {
      const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
      canvas.width = poster.offsetWidth * 2;
      canvas.height = poster.offsetHeight * 2;
      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
      ctx.scale(2, 2);
      ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0);
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.download = 'final_poster.png';
      link.href = canvas.toDataURL('image/png');
      link.click();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    };
    img.src = url;
  };
  document.body.appendChild(btn);
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
