232	        <p>The global economy has demonstrated notable resilience in the face of heightened trade tensions and policy uncertainty. Last year's faster-than-expected growth capped a recovery from the 2020 recession that is <strong>unmatched in six decades</strong>. However, this headline resilience masks a widening gap: vulnerable emerging market and developing economies (EMDEs) continue to lag significantly behind advanced economies. Global growth is projected to edge downward this year, driven by firms scaling back inventory accumulation and the intensifying effects of tariffs.</p>
